  "comment": "The vectors pinning Prima.WorkerAPI as it crosses HTTP (Prima.WorkerWire): every request CYFR makes of a worker service, signed with the dispatch key of tests/fixtures/worker_auth.json under its fields (Prima.WorkerAuth.request_header/3) and posted plain, and its plain answer. Every body and answer carries v, the wire version, as its first member; a body whose v is absent or not version is unknown_version before its op is read, and an answer without it, or at another, is a lost answer. refusals are the answers each request may be given instead, at their HTTP status, with why: a 503 is a refusal of a start only when it names a sentence, and is otherwise a lost answer. status holds the vectors of a status answer's value.",
